  "question": {
    "text": "A wire of resistance R is bent into an equilateral triangle and an identical wire is bent into $a$ square. The ratio of resistance between the two end points of an edge of the triangle to that of the square is\nOptions",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "P3GuV",
      "text": "8/9",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "5COLk",
      "text": "$27 / 32$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "eH5CI",
      "text": "$32 / 27$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "iDlof",
      "text": "$9 / 8$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For the wire bent into an equilateral triangle, each side has a resistance $\\frac{R}{3}$.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/K_k2zGFxLJ3eLJlxsX7dg1x1amevucLIUZEZFL6Ioqw.original.fullsize.png\">\n$R_{\\text {eq }}=\\frac{\\left(\\frac{2 R}{3}\\right)\\left(\\frac{R}{3}\\right)}{\\frac{2 R}{3}+\\frac{R}{3}}=\\frac{2 R}{9}=R_1$ (lets say)\nFor the wire bent into a square, each side has a resistance $\\frac{R}{4}$.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/DMomNIulDwj5wPsA5Yqu-QDOWLMCDVlijXTSTb1VnSI.original.fullsize.png\">\n$\\begin{aligned} & R_{\\text {eq }}=\\frac{\\left(\\frac{3 R}{4}\\right)\\left(\\frac{R}{4}\\right)}{\\frac{3 R}{4}+\\frac{R}{4}}=\\frac{3 R}{16}=R_3 \\text { (lets say) } \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\frac{R_1}{R_3}=\\frac{\\frac{2 R}{9}}{\\frac{3 R}{16}}=\\frac{32}{27}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
